Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 68 year old woman with a history of left breast invasive ductal carcinoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is no residual invasive or in situ carcinoma present  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm oriented left breast simple mastectomy specimen  The specimen is oriented  per the surgeon  by a visible cavity on the posterior surface of the specimen indicating the 9 o clock position  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse that contains an areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple that are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 8cm cavity in the upper outer quadrant  At the lateral aspect of the cavity  there is a firm area  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm irregular tissue that is 1cm to the closest posterior and 2cm to the closest anterior margins  Extending posteriorly from the cavity  there is firm area extending to the posterior margin  Also surrounding the cavity there are areas of bright yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  In the lower   inferior   quadrant  there is ill defined  1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6 cm hemorrhagic tissue that is 6cm to the closest posterior and 1 8cm to the closest anterior margins  The remainder of the breast is fibrous  Also within the same container there are three unoriented  unremarkable fragments of skin that aggregate to 14 x 9 x 0 6cm  No lymph nodes are grossly appreciated in the upper outer quadrant  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast near skin in the central area of the breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of firm tissue at the lateral aspect of the cavity to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of bright yellow discoloration adjacent to cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of firm tissue extending from cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire hemorrhagic area in lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative breast parenchyma from lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from central area  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 58 45PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , No.
