cavity is located within the mid to inferior aspect of the specimen and is located 0 6cm from the black inked posterior aspect and 1 5cm from the overlying scar bearing skin  The cavity lining is tan pink  focally hemorrhagic smooth and glistening  The cavity borders are indurated and grossly unremarkable  Located 4 0cm superior lateral is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ill defined  tan white centrally hemorrhagic irregular area that comes to 1 5cm from the black inked posterior margin and 2 2cm from the anterior skin surface  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma consist of tan yellow pink  lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified  The most lateral and superior aspect at the posterior margin is a slightly indurated  REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm area displaying a smooth and glistening dark red to tan fibrotic surface rimmed by tan yellow tissue  Lymph nodes are not identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Closest extent of cavity to posterior margin  B  Closest extent of cavity to anterior skin margin with scar  C D  Representative sections of cavity wall  E  Separate lateral nodule to deep margin  F G  Uninvolved parenchyma  H I  Fibrotic smooth walled cavity at posterior aspect  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , No.
